  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nA strong upper trough will keep cool conditions through tonight \nbefore weakening and allowing temperatures climb closer to normal \nby Wednesday. Tonight low temperatures look to drop below \nfreezing with clearing skies and light wind. With these cooler \ntemperatures, make sure to protect sensitive vegetation.\n\nBy mid week upper level ridging over the west coast will allow\nquick moving shortwave troughs to sneak through the overall quasi-\nzonal flow, bringing some isolated thunderstorm chances through \nthe end of the weeeeek (get it? it's like a rollercoaster). The \nbest chance for thunderstorms will be Wednesday. Model plumes \ncontinue to suggest weak instability in the ~300 J/kg MLCAPE range\nduring Wednesday evening. GEFS forecast RH and dewpoint for \nWednesday evening continue to rise.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nNo changes to NBM.",
